      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The biosynthesis of the azabicyclic ring system of the azinomycin family of antitumor agents represents the \"crown jewel\" of the pathway and is a complex process involving at least 14 enzymatic steps. This study reports on the first biosynthetic step, the inroads, in the construction of the novel aziridino [1,2-a]pyrrolidine, azabicyclic core, allowing us to support a new mechanism for azabicycle formation."},
